K-58\\n\\n# Slack Thread: High-DPI Upstream Block\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:41] Diana**: Bad news on the high-DPI rendering fix. The rotation fix Charlie pushed works for simple cases, but it's completely breaking on documents with nested Form XObjects.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:43] Charlie**: Yeah, I looked into it. The underlying rendering library we're using (`pdf-lib-core`) has a known bug in how it handles coordinates for XObjects when a parent transform is applied.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:55] Alice**: Can we patch it?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:56] Charlie**: No.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:35] Charlie**: It's deep in their C++ core. I've opened an issue with the upstream maintainers, but they haven't responded.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:37] Evan**: We can't wait for an upstream fix if we're hitting the release gate. Can we work around it by flattening the PDFs first?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:51] Charlie**: Flattening might work but it'll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layers.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:29] Alice**: @Diana, @Charlie, let's leave high-DPI rendering blocked for now. We need to decide if we can ship with this limitation or if we need a different rendering library entirely.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:32] Diana**: Agreed. It only affects a small subset of complex documents, but we should document it as a known issue.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 58 slack thread high dpi upstream block channel cipherdoc date 2026 09 10 2026 09 1010 41 diana bad news on the high dpi render fix the rotat fix charli push work for simpl case but it s complet break on document with nest form xobject 2026 09 1010 43 charli yeah i look into it the under render librari we re use pdf lib core ha a known bug in how it handl coordin for xobject when a parent transform is appli 2026 09 1010 55 alic can we patch it 2026 09 1010 56 charli no 2026 09 10 11 35 charli it s deep in their c core i ve open an issu with the upstream maintain but they haven t respond 2026 09 10 11 37 evan we can t wait for an upstream fix if we re hit the releas gate can we work around it by flatten the pdfs first 2026 09 10 11 51 charli flatten might work but it ll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layer 2026 09 10 12 29 alic diana charli let s leav high dpi render block for now we need to decid if we can ship with this limit or if we need a differ render librari entir 2026 09 10 12 32 diana agre it onli affect a small subset of complex document but we should document it a a known issu\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9310f048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"id\": \"72425f09d11fcc84\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33804571082325663, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17815263689036662, \"vector_similarity\": 0.71112955, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9310f048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1371, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:29\", \"token_count\": 414, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-08\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Windows & License Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nCharlie opened on the AGPL PDF-parser problem and the search for an Apache/MIT alternative. Evan noted the earlier Windows path fix; code-signing cert procurement remains open.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-08\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Windows & License Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Charlie**: Licensing first — the replacement PDF parser Evan swapped in turned out to be AGPL. I've started searching for an Apache or MIT alternative. Need to confirm feature coverage before we swap again.\\n\\n**Diana**: Right — AGPL isn't acceptable for how we're distributing the toolkit.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Unknown how much rework another swap costs until I compare candidates. That's this week's task. I'd rather not guess.\\n\\n**Evan**: Separate note while we're all here — the Windows backslash path handling fix from earlier this month has been holding up fine in the build. No regressions there.\\n\\n**Alice**: Good to hear. And signing?\\n\\n**Evan**: Still waiting on the code-signing certificate to come through procurement. No firm timeline yet, so I can't say when that's cleared.\\n\\n**Alice**: Okay — Charlie, keep pushing on the parser alternative, that's the priority. Evan, keep chasing procurement on the cert, but no need for a deep-dive there today.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 08 firefli transcript window licens sync date 2026 08 15 particip alic pm charli engin diana qa evan devop summari charli open on the agpl pdf parser problem and the search for an apach mit altern evan note the earlier window path fix code sign cert procur remain open sourc id src meet 08 firefli transcript window licens sync date 2026 08 15 particip alic pm charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript charli licens first the replac pdf parser evan swap in turn out to be agpl i ve start search for an apach or mit altern need to confirm featur coverag befor we swap again diana right agpl isn t accept for how we re distribut the toolkit charli unknown how much rework anoth swap cost until i compar candid that s this week s task i d rather not guess evan separ note while we re all here the window backslash path handl fix from earlier this month ha been hold up fine in the build no regress there alic good to hear and sign evan still wait on the code sign certif to come through procur no firm timelin yet so i can t say when that s clear alic okay charli keep push on the parser altern that s the prioriti evan keep chase procur on the cert but no need for a deep dive there today\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e951fd048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-15-Windows-License-Sync.md\", \"id\": \"5bd1df00b489f9f3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33456892572433666, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1705609510347667, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7172542, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-15-Windows-License-Sync.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e951fd048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-15-Windows-License-Sync.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-15-Windows-License-Sync.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1335, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:03\", \"token_count\": 372, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Original Finding: Ghostscript (AGPLv3)\\n\\nThe initial audit flagged `Ghostscript`, used by the `rasterizer` module for PDF-to-image conversion, as AGPLv3-licensed — on the corporate license blacklist because of its viral copyleft terms for any binary distributed to partner sites.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## First Remediation and Reopen\\n\\nThe team swapped in an alternative PDF parser library to replace the Ghostscript dependency, and that swap was initially marked Completed. On follow-up review, however, the replacement library itself turned out to also be AGPL-licensed — the swap solved the specific Ghostscript dependency but reintroduced the same license category problem one layer down. The task was reopened.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Current Status: Unresolved\\n\\nCharlie is now searching for an Apache 2.0 or MIT-licensed PDF parser alternative that meets the module's rasterization requirements. No suitable replacement has been confirmed yet, so this audit item remains **Active (Reopened)** — not resolved.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Secondary Open Item\\n\\nTesseract OCR itself is Apache 2.0, but the `eng.traineddata` model files were sourced from a community repository and their training-corpus provenance has not been verified as public-domain/CC0. This remains a separate, lower-priority open item pending Evan's trace of the `tessdata_best` provenance.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 origin find ghostscript agplv3 the initi audit flag ghostscript use by the raster modul for pdf to imag convers a agplv3 licens on the corpor licens blacklist becaus of it viral copyleft term for ani binari distribut to partner site sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 first remedi and reopen the team swap in an altern pdf parser librari to replac the ghostscript depend and that swap wa initi mark complet on follow up review howev the replac librari itself turn out to also be agpl licens the swap solv the specif ghostscript depend but reintroduc the same licens categori problem one layer down the task wa reopen sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 current status unresolv charli is now search for an apach 20 or mit licens pdf parser altern that meet the modul s raster requir no suitabl replac ha been confirm yet so this audit item remain activ reopen not resolv sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 secondari open item tesseract ocr itself is apach 20 but the eng traineddata model file were sourc from a communiti repositori and their train corpus proven ha not been verifi a public domain cc0 this remain a separ lower prioriti open item pend evan s trace of the tessdata _ best proven\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9d4f0568a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"id\": \"039b629d788751dd\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33273045106304916, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1411707272329274, \"vector_similarity\": 0.77970314, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9d4f0568a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1689, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:12\", \"token_count\": 582, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-49\\n\\n# Technical Report: High-DPI Coordinate Scaling — Upstream Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2049\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n## Background\\n\\nEarlier work (2026-08-17) reproduced misalignment on 4K displays. Follow-on scaling math (2026-08-19) was checked against the Completed preview-overlay coordinates from T023.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-49\\n\\n# Technical Report: High-DPI Coordinate Scaling — Upstream Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2049\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n## Finding\\n\\nThe scaling error points to a defect in the upstream rendering library's scaling math. No safe local fix has been identified yet.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-49\\n\\n# Technical Report: High-DPI Coordinate Scaling — Upstream Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2049\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n## Current Status: Blocked\\n\\nT036 is Blocked on that upstream library issue. Local coordinate work remains dependent on T023's overlay path but cannot clear the gate until upstream scaling is corrected or an accepted local remediation is chosen.\\n\\n*Status*: Blocked on upstream rendering-library scaling math.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 49 technic report high dpi coordin scale upstream block owner diana document key doc 2049 last updat 2026 09 10 background earlier work 2026 08 17 reproduc misalign on 4k display follow on scale math 2026 08 19 wa check against the complet preview overlay coordin from t023 sourc id src gdoc 49 technic report high dpi coordin scale upstream block owner diana document key doc 2049 last updat 2026 09 10 find the scale error point to a defect in the upstream render librari s scale math no safe local fix ha been identifi yet sourc id src gdoc 49 technic report high dpi coordin scale upstream block owner diana document key doc 2049 last updat 2026 09 10 current status block t036 is block on that upstream librari issu local coordin work remain depend on t023 s overlay path but can not clear the gate until upstream scale is correct or an accept local remedi is chosen status block on upstream render librari scale math\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9c0f8ee8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-10-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Coordinates-Report.md\", \"id\": \"e9d46560d0ce6c2f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3273016354926129, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16345752498944696, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70960456, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-10-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Coordinates-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9c0f8ee8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-10-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Coordinates-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-10-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Coordinates-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 808, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:25\", \"token_count\": 306, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nPre-release gate review: Docker slim/CVE, Windows signing, and upstream high-DPI remain open. Audit-log path still a hold — CLI schema and emitted records don't match.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Alice**: We're in pre-release mode. Gate check first: Docker slim-down and CVE work is still open, Windows signing is still open, and we're still blocked upstream on the high-DPI rendering bug. Those stay on the board. Diana, where are we on the audit-log gate?\\n\\n**Diana**: Still a hold. The CLI path and the log records aren't matching the schema we defined. That undercuts the audit trail as release evidence.\\n\\n**Bob**: I've been wiring audit-log generation into the CLI. The shape coming out still isn't consistent with what the schema expects — I've got another pass queued.\\n\\n**Charlie**: So this isn't a packaging issue — it's schema versus emitted records?\\n\\n**Diana**: Yes. Until those match, I can't clear the audit gate.\\n\\n**Evan**: That stacks on top of the Docker and Windows holds Alice listed. Release isn't opening with any of those unresolved.\\n\\n**Alice**: Correct. Security-gate work stays open — Docker slim-down, Windows signing, and we keep the audit mismatch visible as a release blocker. No one closes those today.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep the audit-log gate red until schema and records match.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari pre releas gate review docker slim cve window sign and upstream high dpi remain open audit log path still a hold cli schema and emit record don t match sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript alic we re in pre releas mode gate check first docker slim down and cve work is still open window sign is still open and we re still block upstream on the high dpi render bug those stay on the board diana where are we on the audit log gate diana still a hold the cli path and the log record aren t match the schema we defin that undercut the audit trail a releas evid bob i ve been wire audit log generat into the cli the shape come out still isn t consist with what the schema expect i ve got anoth pas queu charli so this isn t a packag issu it s schema versus emit record diana yes until those match i can t clear the audit gate evan that stack on top of the docker and window hold alic list releas isn t open with ani of those unresolv alic correct secur gate work stay open docker slim down window sign and we keep the audit mismatch visibl a a releas blocker no one close those today diana i ll keep the audit log gate red until schema and record match\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"id\": \"be17298264309b61\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3213856654926128, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16345752498944696, \"vector_similarity\": 0.68988466, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1495, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:06\", \"token_count\": 424, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"2026-09-22 release license gate PDF parser AGPL Apache MIT rasterization clean scan\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"As of 2026-09-22, the license gate remains **Active (Reopened)**—not cleared for release. The full dependency tree still must be compliant, and the shipped set may not contain restrictive copyleft licenses. [SRC-CU-CIPH-40]\n\nIt was reopened by a follow-up license-file check: the replacement PDF parser, installed to remediate the original Ghostscript/AGPLv3 finding, was itself AGPL-licensed. That is incompatible with the current distribution model. [SRC-SLACK-40] [SRC-GDOC-41]\n\nThe replacement must:\n\n- Be licensed under **Apache 2.0 or MIT** (i.e., non-copyleft).\n- Meet the module’s required PDF parsing/rasterization functionality.\n- Be adopted and pass a clean dependency-license scan, with no restrictive copyleft remaining in the shipped dependency set. [SRC-GDOC-41] [SRC-CU-CIPH-40]\n\nNo suitable replacement had been confirmed in the available sources; earlier candidates lacked full feature coverage. [SRC-SLACK-41]"}}
